Size reverse_index in tddfpt_guess_vectors by the spin components that exist. nmo has maxspins = 2
entries and the loop that fills it runs over nspins, so in a closed-shell run nmo(2) is never set and
MAXVAL(nmo(:)) takes whatever the stack holds: 1068944951 in a GCC 15.2.0 build for Sapphire Rapids,
for which every MPI rank allocated and zeroed 4 GiB on each call of the TDDFPT initial guess.
Author: Rohit Goswami
--- cp2k-2026.2.orig/src/qs_tddfpt2_utils.F
+++ cp2k-2026.2/src/qs_tddfpt2_utils.F
@@ -1122,4 +1122,4 @@
-      i = MAXVAL(nmo(:))
+      i = MAXVAL(nmo(1:nspins))
       ALLOCATE (reverse_index(i, nspins))
       reverse_index = 0
       DO ispin = 1, nspins
